Z||000000||bilbo||01-29-2001||06:11 PM||||Someone told me that if you disconnect your a/c compressor and put a free flowing belt pulley in it's place you'll gain some horsies.....anyone know if this true???!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-29-2001||06:18 PM||||Absolutely positively not true. When the compressor is not engaged the pulley is just spinning on a bearing and is not connected to anything. If you take the belt off you can spin it easily with you hand and see for yourself. Taking the belt off will only leave you with no AC and nothing else. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bilbo||01-29-2001||06:21 PM||||Thanks 88 Formula,guess I'll be keepin my a/c then!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||01-29-2001||07:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bilbo:<BR><B>Someone told me that if you disconnect your a/c compressor and put a free flowing belt pulley in it's place you'll gain some horsies.....anyone know if this true???!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The advice that 88 Formula gave you on this is 100% correct.<P>I'd like to comment on the person who told you to do it in the first place. <P>It never ceases to amaze me how many people are out there passing out Rotten, Stupid, mis-informed advice. The must be talking just to hear themselves talk. People like that ought to be slapped up side the head. <P>In fact, next time you see him, you should give him a good "smack" up side the head. When he asks you why you did that, just tell him "Someone told me" to do it.<P>Archie||||reg||10
