Z||000007||Standard||01-30-2001||01:45 AM||||what they said...<P>but you can gain a little speed by taking out the A/C system, which is what I plan on doing since mine doesn't work and I never use it anyways.  I like driving with the sunroof off too much, and I'd rather not waste the power and gas to drive the compressor.. 'course, maybe when I'm old I'll change my mind  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> no offense to all ya' old guys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||
Z||000008||hugh||01-30-2001||07:31 AM||||The only reason you may gain a little speed by taking out the air conditioning system is you are lightning the car.The effects you get probably won't even be measurable.If the air isn't on all you are doing is spinning the compressor clutch pulley.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||01-30-2001||09:52 AM||||You dont have to remove your AC components, you can just evacuate all of the R-12 or R-134 and pressurize the system with Helium.  The lighter than air properties of the helium will offset the weight of the AC components so you can keep your AC but not worry about all that added weight. <P>At least thats what I heard....(kidding)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||2
Z||000010||Greg Piet||01-30-2001||10:35 AM||||Spinning the AC pulley and clutch does take a wee bit o' power, lets be honest now all of you... it IS a rotating mass, and the bearings are not frictionless.  The effects may be inmeasurable which I will not argue about.  Removing the entire system reduces weight, which will get you a faster time...  weight IS weight, and the less of it one has the more one can accelerate with the same motor setup.  <P>But this is likely only beneficial for those looking for that thousandth of a second. <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||01-30-2001||09:03 PM||||When a fly hits your windshield it actually slows your car down a little although that is not measurable either is it? Better not hit any bugs while your racing or your going to lose.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
